# =============================================================================
# INC-16-P5 — canonical REQUIRED env keys for the AWS orchestration box.
#
# The single source of truth for "what must be set (non-empty) in the box .env".
# Two consumers:
#   * CI (scripts/ci/check_env_parity.py) — asserts every key here is documented
#     in services/dagster/aws/.env.example (template completeness).
#   * CD (services/dagster/aws/deploy.sh) — asserts every key here is present AND
#     NON-EMPTY in the box's .env before (re)deploying. ⚠️ `KEY=` (empty) is
#     treated as MISSING — an empty value SHADOWS a script's code default
#     (os.environ.get(k, default) returns "" when present-but-empty), which is
#     exactly how P4 lost cycles to CACHE_BUCKET / USER_BETS_TABLE.
#
# Format: one KEY per line; blank lines and `#` comments ignored.
# Keep in sync when an op starts reading a new required env var.
# =============================================================================

# --- Dagster metadata PG (compose-internal) ---
DAGSTER_PG_PASSWORD

# --- Snowflake (OLAP / dbt-runner / ops) ---
SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT
SNOWFLAKE_USER
SNOWFLAKE_ROLE
SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE
SNOWFLAKE_PRIVATE_KEY

# --- AWS region (region-less boto3 = empty endpoint; P2 bug) ---
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION

# --- dbt-runner ---
DBT_RUNNER_AUTH_TOKEN
DBT_STATE_BUCKET
DBT_STATE_PREFIX
TARGET_ENV

# --- Serving cache (DynamoDB + S3 fallback) — P2/P4 ---
SERVING_CACHE_TABLE
CACHE_BUCKET

# --- Sub-model artifacts from S3 under instance profile (P4) ---
ARTIFACTS_FROM_S3

# --- DynamoDB user-bet settlement (P4) ---
USER_BETS_TABLE
USERS_TABLE

# --- Sports (NCAAF/NFL) DuckDB — NF-INFRA1 -----------------------------------
# MUST be /var/lib/credence/sports/sports.duckdb — the `sports_duckdb` NAMED VOLUME mounted on
# dagster-codeloc. Required here (present AND non-empty) because an UNSET value is exactly the
# defect: with no env var, four owners each fell back to their own default (`/tmp/…`, `/app/…`,
# profiles.yml's) and the whole NFL build chain read a file nothing wrote — 19 consecutive green
# runs over a 19-day-dead Sleeper feed (NF-FRESH1). `/tmp` is wiped by every deploy and `/app` is
# replaced by the image, so ONLY a path inside the volume survives.
# Single owner: betting_ml/utils/sports_duckdb.py (BOX_DUCKDB_PATH). See BOX_OPERATIONS.md §10a.
# ⚠️ A `git pull` never touches the box's .env — adding this key is a MANUAL operator step, and
# the next deploy FAILS until it is there (that gate is the point).
SPORTS_DUCKDB_PATH

# --- Odds feed (capture ops) ---
ODDS_API_KEY
# NOTE: OPENWEATHERMAP_API_KEY is intentionally NOT required — it only enables the
# OPTIONAL OpenWeatherMap fallback in ingest_weather.py (WARN-tier op; weather is
# closed as noise for totals). The box runs fine without it; kept in .env.example
# as an optional, documented key.

# --- dagit HTTPS + basic-auth (Caddy) — P4 ---
DAGIT_HOSTNAME
DAGIT_BASIC_AUTH_USER
DAGIT_BASIC_AUTH_HASH

# --- Observability alert channel (P6) — the shared SNS topic everything pages to.
# Required so alerting isn't silently dark (the notifier soft-fails if unset). Set
# from provision-observability.sh's printed ARN BEFORE the first P6 deploy.
ALERT_SNS_TOPIC_ARN

# --- Permanently-on lakehouse-cutover flags (E11.23) — MUST be "1" ------------
# The E11.1 cutover left a class of RUNTIME failures CI can't see: an intraday
# refresh shipped gated-off / a flag left unset silently degrades serving with NO
# alert (odds froze 3 days). check_monitors_healthy_op alarms at RUNTIME if any of
# these is not "1"; listing them here escalates that to a DEPLOY-TIME gate — a box
# .env missing/emptying one FAILS the deploy (rollback) instead of shipping degraded.
# ⚠️ env.required checks present-AND-non-empty only; the "== 1" value is enforced by
# the runtime guard. Keep in sync with monitor_health.REQUIRED_INTRADAY_FLAGS + BOX_OPERATIONS.md §10a.
SCHEDULE_LAKEHOUSE_INTRADAY
LINEUP_INTRADAY_S3_REBUILD
W8A_LAKEHOUSE_S3
W8B_LAKEHOUSE_S3
# E11.20-COST (2026-07-16): W7A/W7B added after W7B was found NEVER SET on the box —
# §10 intended ON since the W7a/W7b cutovers, but as unenforced flags they silently
# drifted (the daily predict/serving read Snowflake for weeks). Same class, same cure.
W7A_LAKEHOUSE_S3
W7B_LAKEHOUSE_S3
# E11.20 phase-2a (2026-07-20): lineup-monitor detection tick reads S3+DynamoDB, not Snowflake.
# Flipped + converged 2026-07-20; enforced so it can't drift off (the W7B lesson).
LINEUP_MONITOR_S3
# E11.20 phase-2a steps 2+4 (2026-07-26): intraday serving/predict → S3 (W7B_INTRADAY_S3, needs
# W6_LAKEHOUSE_INTRADAY) + the 30-min tick skips its SF ext-refresh + dbt-rebuild legs (TICK_SF_FREE)
# = the last high-frequency COMPUTE_WH wakers. Enforced so they can't silently drift back to SF on a
# re-host. ⚠️ TICK_SF_FREE flipped 2026-07-26, in its first soak — a soak rollback must set it 0 AND
# remove it here + from monitor_health.REQUIRED_INTRADAY_FLAGS (else the heartbeat false-pages).
W6_LAKEHOUSE_INTRADAY
W7B_INTRADAY_S3
TICK_SF_FREE
# E11.24 literal-zero-Snowflake (2026-07-31): the stage-1 cost levers. Listed here for PRESENCE
# only — env.required does not pin a VALUE, so this does not force them ON and cannot false-page
# on a deliberate rollback. It closes the W6_ODDS_SF_FREE bite recorded in test_cost_wake_gates.py:
# that flag was ABSENT from the box .env, so the handed-off `sed -i` flip matched nothing, changed
# nothing, and the deploy still SUCCEEDED — "the key isn't in env.required, so no gate caught it."
# An absent key makes "flip it to 1" a silent no-op; presence-enforcement is the cure.
# Verified present + non-empty on the box 2026-07-31 (all three read back =1 from dagster-codeloc).
# ⏭️ Promotion to monitor_health.REQUIRED_INTRADAY_FLAGS (which DOES pin =='1') is a separate,
# later call per flag — see the note there; do not promote a flag still in its first soak.
E11_24_ELO_SF_FREE
E11_24_WEATHER_SF_FREE
E11_24_STATCAST_CATCHUP_GATE
# E11.24 TARGET 6 — the intraday EB/lineup chain levers. PRESENCE only, same as above;
# ships default-OFF and is in its FIRST soak, so it may not be promoted to
# REQUIRED_INTRADAY_FLAGS yet.
#   E11_24_BULLPEN_S3_READ — update_team_posteriors reads its bullpen observations from the S3
#     lakehouse via DuckDB instead of Snowflake, which also removes the ordering dependency that
#     forces the w8b aggregator to mirror a one-slate-stale team_sequential_posteriors.
#
# ⛔ E11_24_UMPIRE_REBUILD_GATE was REMOVED 2026-08-05 (E11.24 target 6). The four ext-table-COPY
#    models it gated are now `materialized='view'` on the Snowflake target, so their rebuild is
#    metadata-only DDL that never resumes COMPUTE_WH — a conditional SKIP of a free operation
#    saves nothing. The gate was independently verified INERT on the 2026-08-04 armed slate
#    (0 skips of 3 real opportunities; its S3 marker object had never existed, so every tick took
#    the fail-OPEN path). Nothing needs doing on the box: env-parity only checks that keys listed
#    HERE are present in .env, so a leftover key there is harmless. Remove it at leisure.
E11_24_BULLPEN_S3_READ
